# FAMILYFI_DEFAULT_PASSWORD, FAMILYFI_SESSION_SECRET and FAMILYFI_ENCRYPTION_KEY
# are optional. On first setup (`make setup` or first container boot) they are
# generated if missing and written to disk. In Docker they persist under
# /var/lib/familyfi/data/.env on the familyfi-app volume. You may pass any of
# them in the process environment to override. Back up FAMILYFI_ENCRYPTION_KEY
# with the database — rotating it without re-saving the UniFi API key breaks
# Sync with "Unsupported state or unable to authenticate data".

# bundled = app + PostgreSQL via docker/docker-compose.yml. external = use DB_HOST below.
# memory = an in-memory database, for dev and test only.
# (The older names DB_MODE and POSTGRES_PORT, POSTGRES_DB, POSTGRES_USER and POSTGRES_PASSWORD
# still work for now, with a warning at startup.)
DB_SERVER=bundled
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=familyfi
DB_USER=familyfi
DB_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Examples: disable, require, verify-full.
# DB_SSL_MODE=require
# DB_SSL_ROOT_CERT=/path/to/ca.pem

# Published host port for `make docker-up` (container listens on 7001).
FAMILYFI_PORT=7001

# Optional override for `make docker-up`.
# FAMILYFI_IMAGE=ghcr.io/nickberardi/familyfi:latest

# Remote access through a tunnel sidecar container (docs/setup.md). Exposes the phone-only
# gateway to other containers on the Compose network; never publish it on the host.
# FAMILYFI_PHONE_GATEWAY_PORT=7002

# The kind of work this process does (docs/setup.md#modes): prod (default, a real gateway),
# dev (the UniFi mock and a dummy household, for local UI work; add DB_SERVER=memory for an
# in-memory database), test (automated runs), or demo (the public demo, docs/operations.md#demo-mode).
# Production starts only prod and demo.
# FAMILYFI_MODE=dev
# The demo's public HTTPS origin, published as the phones' route.
# FAMILYFI_DEMO_URL=https://demo.example.com

# The spike CLI (`make spike`) reads its own SPIKE_* settings; see docs/spike/OPERATOR.md.
